course: dictionary
lesson: 7986
title: Recovery: getting better and getting back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Recovery is a noun, and it means getting better after being ill, hurt or upset. «Quiet rest, like reading, drawing or sleeping, helps recovery» tells you that rest helps your body get better. The clue is the word helps, which shows that recovery is something that happens over time.
explain: The same word can mean getting something back. «Breakdown recovery is a service that sends someone to fix a broken-down car or tow it to a garage.» Here recovery means bringing back something that was broken or lost, not a person getting well.
explain: Look at the words next to recovery. «A full recovery» means completely better, and «on the road to recovery» means getting better step by step. Try your meaning in the sentence: if «a full recovery» means «completely better» and the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Recovery means getting better after being ill, hurt or upset.
fact: «A full recovery» means getting completely better.
fact: «Breakdown recovery» is a service that tows a broken-down car to a garage.
fact: Recovery can also mean getting useful materials back from rubbish, as in recycling.
fact: Quiet rest helps recovery, and «a second infection» can make you worse again just when you felt better.
exercise: «After her flu she made a full recovery.» What does full recovery mean? | Ill again | *Completely better | Lost in bed | Still feeling ill
exercise: «The breakdown recovery van towed our car to the garage.» What is a breakdown recovery van for? | Delivering the post | Carrying people on holiday | Taking children to school | *Fixing or towing a broken-down car
exercise: «The team made a recovery from 2–0 down.» What does recovery mean here? | Stopped playing for the day | *Got back into the game after a bad time | Went home early | Lost the game by even more
test: «Quiet rest, like reading or sleeping, helps recovery.» What helps recovery, according to this sentence? | Skipping meals | *Quiet rest, like reading or sleeping | Running a race straight after being ill | Staring at screens late at night
test: «Resource recovery» means getting useful materials back from rubbish. Which is an example of resource recovery? | Burning a forest | *Turning old bottles into new ones | Throwing paper in the bin | Leaving broken toys on the street
exam: Which meaning of recovery fits a stolen bike that the police find and return? | *Getting back something that was lost or stolen | Throwing rubbish away | Breaking down on the road | Getting better after being ill
